    },
    "body": "The fixed reader adaptation does not support promoting either transferred radial configuration. After the same 1,024 updates and 4,194,304 new target visits per arm, Dot has lower full-development NLL and more complete source answers than Lorentz or Affine. Preserve Lorentz's small greedy-story gain and the concrete source tradeoffs; park these configurations without a dose, seed or decoder sweep.\n\nThis records the completed three fits, six Read/NoRead evaluations and joined comparison, including source/binary/final-weight identities, all compact generated outputs, independent prose judgments, resource receipts and cumulative accounting. It updates the README, current state and roadmap, and selects an integrated complete-prefix versus role-only dialogue learner as the next implementation. That new fit is NOT_RUN; the native multiplier-free serving target and accepted integer parents remain unchanged.\n\nValidation: the frozen Rust pipeline completed and verified all report/checkpoint seals; all nine supervised model processes exited zero without resource stops. Independent review recomputed all 27 paired population deltas/counts and 976 block means from the seven row files, checked all 96 new Read source responses, and reviewed all 30 new Read prose stories. The publication packet's 78 file bindings and local document links were checked. `git diff --check` and `python3 scripts/check_claim_wording.py` pass. This PR changes documentation/evidence only; the existing Rust checks were not rerun. Merge-queue compatibility acknowledgements are not test results.\n\nReferences #973 and #820.\n",
